SELECT 
  policy_no, claim_no, 
  GDW_RDM_ANNUAL_STATEMENT_LINE_CD AS class_cd,
  GDW_LINE_OF_BUSINESS_CD AS lob,
  DIVISION_NO AS division,
  SECTION_CD AS section,
  PROFIT_UNIT_CD AS profit_unit,
  SYSTEM_ID, COVERAGE_CODE, SRM_OUTGOING_TRANSACTION_ID
FROM stage_misreg.STAGE_SRM_PREMIUM_LOSS
WHERE policy_no IN ('0041000566','0041000706');
✅ Goal: Confirm metadata consistency after code changes.

3. Date Validations
Ensure effective and expiration dates are valid:

sql
Copy
Edit
SELECT 
  policy_no, claim_no,
  POLICY_EFF_DT, POLICY_EXP_DT,
  TRAN_EFF_DT, TRAN_EXP_DT,
  COVERAGE_EFF_DT, COVERAGE_EXP_DT
FROM stage_misreg.STAGE_SRM_PREMIUM_LOSS
WHERE policy_no IN ('0041000566','0041000706')
  AND (
    POLICY_EXP_DT < POLICY_EFF_DT
    OR TRAN_EXP_DT < TRAN_EFF_DT
    OR COVERAGE_EXP_DT < COVERAGE_EFF_DT
  );
⚠️ Goal: Identify bad date sequences (should return zero rows post-fix).

4. Premium Amounts and Effective Dates
Join with your transaction/date tables to fetch and verify:

sql
Copy
Edit
SELECT
  p.policy_no,
  t.premium_am,
  d.actual_dt AS effective_date
FROM misreg.ttransaction t
JOIN misreg.tdate d ON t.effective_dt_sk = d.date_sk
JOIN misreg.tpolicy p ON t.policy_sk = p.policy_sk
WHERE p.policy_no IN ('0041000566','0041000706')
  AND t.premium_am <> 0;
✅ Goal: Check that premium amounts and dates align with staging.

5. Transaction Amounts (trans_am)
Aggregate and inspect transactions for premium recovery or loss:

sql
Copy
Edit
SELECT
  policy_no,
  claim_no,
  TRAN_EFF_DT,
  ACCOUNTING_DT,
  sum(TRAN_AM) AS total_trans_amt,
  PREMIUM_LOSS_IND
FROM stage_misreg.STAGE_SRM_PREMIUM_LOSS
WHERE policy_no IN ('0041000566','0041000706')
GROUP BY
  policy_no, claim_no, TRAN_EFF_DT, ACCOUNTING_DT, PREMIUM_LOSS_IND;
✅ Goal: Confirm amounts add up and the PREMIUM_LOSS_IND flags correctly.

6. Compare with External Feed (FISERV)
Match staging data with CIP feed values for inception and recovery:

sql
